  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v2.1.9 (IMPORTANT — supersedes 2.1.8 for any product that must work offline): going offline no longer invalidates the offline licence. The machine fingerprint includes the MAC address, which is only readable while a network adapter is up; disabling the network turned it into \"UNKNOWN_MAC\", the fingerprint string changed, and an exact comparison then rejected a genuinely signed, valid licence. The fallback to the on-disk cache could not save it either, because the cache encryption key was derived from the same fingerprint, so the file could no longer be decrypted. A product taken offline therefore lost its licence at the moment it went offline, rather than at the end of the period the platform had signed for. This release introduces a separate stable fingerprint (CPU, motherboard, machine GUID, volume serial — no MAC) which the cache key is derived from, and accepts a fingerprint difference only when all three hold at once: an anchor was recorded while the machine was fully measurable, the only unreadable part is the volatile component, and every stable component matches exactly. The wire fingerprint sent to and signed by the platform is unchanged, so existing signed envelopes keep verifying. Rejections now name the product they concern, so a diagnostic log can be attributed.\nv2.1.8: \"Could not ask\" is no longer reported to the product as \"no licence\" — a new LicenseResult.Unavailable carries the transient case (User Panel not running, channel silent, client-side rate limit) separately from a platform denial, so a product can stop gating features forever and stop prompting to buy a licence the user already owns. The cached verdict now has its own per-product store keyed by ProductKey: offline works without an active lease and survives a restart, which previously it did not for free products. The on-disk cache record is merged rather than replaced by whichever writer touched it last — lease renewal no longer erases ProductKey and the offline expiry, which used to break offline degradation from the very first renewal. A cached status is raised only on proof, never by default. The panel's answer budget is now derived from the channel timeout (IpcProtocol.HandlerBudgetMs) instead of being an independent number, so the panel cannot think for longer than the product is willing to wait. Half-connectivity (captive portal) is read as absence of network rather than as a server denial.\nv2.1.7: Offline grace now lasts the full period the server signed (cacheValidUntil, 7 days) instead of being cut to 24 hours by the live-path replay window; a failed signature or integrity check no longer deletes the cached licence, so a single transient failure can no longer destroy the only offline artefact. Adds a second trusted central-key thumbprint, so replacing the signing key no longer requires every user to reinstall. Reports the plugin version to the platform on license validation (diagnostics only, no version gating).",
